<p>The Australian Government 5% Deposit Scheme lets an eligible first home buyer purchase with a deposit of 5% and pay no Lenders Mortgage Insurance (LMI). The government, through Housing Australia, guarantees the lender up to 15% of the property value. It used to be called the First Home Guarantee. The catch is a bigger loan, and a strict set of rules on price, occupancy and lenders.</p>
<p>I see this most with Sydney professionals who earn well but have not saved 20%. For many, it is the first door to check.</p>
<h2>What the scheme is</h2>
<p>You put in at least 5%. Housing Australia guarantees the lender up to 15% of the property value. That lets you borrow up to 95% of the value without LMI.</p>
<p>The guarantee protects the lender, not you. It does not cover missed repayments. If the home is sold because you cannot pay, you can still owe money after the sale.</p>
<p>The scheme has two streams now:</p>
{% call v.compare("av-compare--pair") %}
{% call v.card("", "oak") %}
<p><strong>The main stream.</strong> For first home buyers, in cities and regions alike. The separate Regional First Home Buyer Guarantee closed to new applicants from 1 October 2025, so regional buyers use the main stream.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% call v.card("", "ink") %}
<p><strong>Single Parents and Legal Guardians.</strong> This replaced the Family Home Guarantee. The deposit is 2% and the guarantee is up to 18%. You do not need to be a first home buyer. You must apply alone and own no other property after settlement.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
<h2>Who is eligible</h2>
<p>For the main stream, you need to be:</p>
{% call v.checklist() %}
<li>An Australian citizen or permanent resident when the loan is signed. A pending visa does not count.</li>
<li>18 or older.</li>
<li>A first home buyer, or someone who has not held an interest in Australian property in the past 10 years.</li>
<li>Buying a home to live in. You must move in within 6 months of settlement (or of the occupancy certificate for a new build) and keep living there while the guarantee is in place.</li>
<li>Taking a principal and interest loan of up to 30 years (interest-only is allowed only in limited cases, such as construction).</li>
{% endcall %}
<p>You can apply alone or with one other person. That can be a partner, a friend or a family member. Both of you must qualify.</p>
<p>Since 1 October 2025 there is no income test and no limit on places. A high salary no longer shuts you out.</p>
<h2>Price caps</h2>
<p>The purchase price and the lender's valuation must both be at or under the cap for the location.</p>
{% call v.note("ink") %}
<p><strong>Price caps as at 1 July 2026.</strong> Caps change. Check the current caps on the <a href="https://www.firsthomebuyers.gov.au/australian-government-5-percent-deposit-scheme/property-price-caps">official property price caps page</a> before you make an offer.</p>
{% endcall %}
